  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A deep profile of the udon VM in the engine shows a significant amount of time being spent in CheckExecutionTimeLimit. I suspect this is being called on each instruction. Since checking the high-resolution system timer can be very expensive (involving system calls, and/or a serializing RDTSC instruction), this should be avoided.\nI would suggest two simple mitigations to help reduce this impact:\n1. First, the execution time limit needs only be to be checked on loops - that is, on backwards branches - because otherwise, the program will eventually halt. Alternately, it could be checked every N instructions.\n2. Second, the execution time limit could be checked using a less precise timer. There could be a second thread that, every second, increments a global atomic counter; the udon VM could read this counter and check against the value observed when execution began.",
